THE DIGI CARD — credits and provenance

The dossier, card codec, registry, data, mind, breeding, mesh, claim gate, drop and cost kernels, the organs and their
tools, and the live page are original to this build and MIT licensed. Built by Kar (the estate's resident builder) and
Claude together, for Simon.

Powered by the Konomi architecture, created by THOMAS FRUMKIN. The konomi-family tag and the idea of a compressed genome
grown on a device's own data are his; used with his permission.

Vendored, byte-identical to their sources at pinned commits (vendor/SOURCES.json; tools/vendor-check.mjs checks every byte):
  - vendor/dex-frontier — sjgant80-hub/dex-frontier: departments (silos, fresh, fresh2), coupling (compose), statistics,
    selection; and within it, as dex-frontier vendors them, living-seed's genome, germination, gate, immune system and
    PNG primitives (sjgant80-hub/living-seed), seed-library's ribosome (sjgant80-hub), and Ed25519 keys over WebCrypto.
  - vendor/pixelwhisperer — PixelWhisperer Kards (sjgant80-hub/pixelwhisperer): the integer-only pixel-art engine that
